# WP agent harness QA loop

Harness QA loop: every-change

After each first-party theme or plugin file write in this turn, run the matching gate on that file before the next edit. Do not batch until the end of the task. Red output is the fix list.

- PHP: `phpcs --standard=phpcs.xml.dist <file>` then `php tools/phpstan/vendor/bin/phpstan analyse -c phpstan.neon.dist --memory-limit=1G <file>`
- Theme JS with `@wordpress/scripts`: `npm run lint:js` in that component on the changed file
- Other first-party JS: `npm --prefix tools/js-lint run lint -- <file>`
- For new or changed observable behavior with an explicit OpenSpec scenario or acceptance criterion and an existing runner, Read `.agents/skills/wordpress-testing/SKILL.md` and add warranted tests once that behavior is executable. Skip tiny wiring/presentation changes and do not invent expected results.
- Run the focused new/failing test, then the suite. If `phpunit.xml.dist` exists: `php tools/phpunit/vendor/bin/phpunit -c phpunit.xml.dist`. If Jest exists: `npm --prefix tools/js-test test`, or the component `test` script. Diagnose test failures against the contract; do not rewrite assertions merely for green.
- JS style debt: still run lint. Do not `--fix` or rewrite a whole file for `linebreak-style`, `prettier/prettier`, `indent`, `space-in-parens`, or `template-curly-spacing` unless the user asked to format. Report that count. Fix syntax, `no-undef`, and issues in lines you added. A repo-wide LF/prettier pass is a separate task.
- Skip Core, third-party plugins, `vendor`, `node_modules`, `build`, minified and hashed bundles
- Do not add new findings to `phpstan-baseline.neon`
- Do not open a browser in this loop. After green gates, on UI tasks only, the harness invokes `wp-browser-sensor`. After the browser pass or skip, on non-tiny first-party PHP, HTML templates, JS, or CSS, the harness invokes `local-code-review`.
